      "properties": {"Node name for S&R": "WeeToddH3ReferenceEncode"},
      "widgets_values": [
        "<Picture 1> defines Little Red Riding Hood's face, red hooded cloak, green dress, age, and realistic appearance. <Picture 2> defines the upright gray wolf's face, fur, round glasses, burgundy granny dress, lace bonnet, and realistic appearance. <Picture 3> defines the real Granny's elderly face, gray hair, glasses, burgundy coat, cream dress, and realistic appearance. <Picture 4> defines the woodsman's face, beard, rugged brown clothing, boots, and hand axe.\n\nintegrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] Live-action cinematic realism, one continuous medium-wide eye-level shot inside Granny's detailed timber cottage at dusk. Little Red Riding Hood from <Picture 1> sits at the left side of a small wooden tea table. The wolf from <Picture 2> sits stiffly in the center wearing his burgundy granny dress, lace bonnet, and round glasses, holding a tiny porcelain teacup. The real Granny from <Picture 3> sits at the right side of the table with a dry, unimpressed expression. The woodsman from <Picture 4> stands just behind them, resting his hand axe safely against his boot. A stone fireplace glows behind the group; copper pans, dried herbs, carved shelves, a checked tablecloth, a teapot, jam, and pastries give the room rich realistic detail. Preserve all four separate identities and costumes without merging them. 0:00-0:02 - Red glances from Granny to the wolf, raises one eyebrow, and asks, <d>[English] Grandma, why is the wolf wearing your glasses?</d> 0:02-0:04 - Granny barely looks up from her tea and replies deadpan, <d>[English] Because he ate the optometrist.</d> 0:04-0:05 - The wolf freezes with the tiny teacup halfway to his mouth. The woodsman slowly lowers his axe and quietly suppresses a laugh. Red stares at the wolf. The camera makes only a very gentle slow push in; everyone remains mostly seated and still, with restrained natural facial motion and accurate lip synchronization.\n\noverall_soundscape: Intimate dry dialogue recorded inside the cottage, with Red's curious young voice followed by Granny's calm deadpan elderly voice. A low fireplace crackle, faint evening wind at the window, a soft porcelain cup clink, subtle clothing movement, and the woodsman's brief suppressed snort are synchronized to the action. No overlapping speech and no wolf dialogue.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: N/A"
      ]
